; worldpersist.eval — a dungeon keeps what happened in it (Michael, 2026-09-24:
; "killed the mummy, left, came back in — the mummy was back").
;
; The level walked out of stays loaded under the world map, and everything that
; replaces it next — a doorway, an ambush on the road, a save loaded — does so
; without stashing. So it is PARKED on the way out, and each of these is a way
; back in that must find the skeleton still dead:
;
;   1. straight back through the gate;
;   2. with a random encounter in between, which REPLACES the level under the
;      world map with a generated one;
;   3. through a save made on the world map, loaded twice: once over the same
;      level (the inline branch) and once over another (the loading branch),
;      because LoadGame finishes the job in two different places.
;
; Every `monsters` after the kill is a measurement; the one before it is the
; control — "dead on re-entry" means nothing unless it was alive to begin with.
logecho on
reset
seed 4
freeze on
leave
discover crypt_gate
enter crypt_gate
echo --- persist: before the kill ---
monsters
blast fireburst 7 4
blast fireburst 7 4
blast fireburst 7 4
blast fireburst 7 4
blast fireburst 7 4
step 1
echo --- persist: killed ---
monsters

; --- 1. out and straight back in -------------------------------------------
leave
enter crypt_gate
echo --- persist: back through the gate ---
monsters

; --- 2. an ambush on the road in between ------------------------------------
leave
worldpos 6 6
encounter
leave
enter crypt_gate
echo --- persist: after an encounter ---
monsters

; --- 3. a save made on the world map ----------------------------------------
leave
save worldpersist
load worldpersist
echo --- persist: loaded over the same level ---
state
enter crypt_gate
monsters
reset
load worldpersist
echo --- persist: loaded over another level ---
state
enter crypt_gate
monsters
